tle": "2026 chemistry Nobel predictions span three research fields", "url": "https://digg.com/science/m57ye2zq"}, {"title": "7 October 2026, Wednesday, 13:41", "url": "https://charter97.org/en/news/2026/10/7/701038/"}, {"title": "THE NOBEL PRIZE IN CHEMISTRY", "url": "https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/chemistry/)"}, {"title": "All Nobel Prizes in Chemistry", "url": "https://www.nobelprize.org/nobel_prizes/chemistry/laureates/index.html"}]}, "The 2026 Nobel Prize in Chemistry went to Henri B. Kagan and Kenso Soai, announced on October 7, 2026. The Nobel Prize site credits them for the discovery of non-linear effects and autocatalysis in asymmetric organic synthesis.\n\n- **Kagan** is based at Université Paris-Sud in Orsay, France. **Soai**, who is 95, is at the Tokyo University of Science. Kagan is associated with Université Paris-Sud in Orsay, France, while Soai, 95, is affiliated with the Tokyo University of Science.\n- **The work:** Their research concerns mirror-image molecules. Kagan's work allowed a greater excess of one of the mirror images to be created than was previously assumed possible. The prize also covers how that handedness could have emerged in the first place, a question the Academy describes as a long-standing puzzle for chemists.\n- **Prize money:** Each Nobel prize this year is worth 12 million Swedish kronor, about $1.2 million, and the chemistry award is split equally between the two laureates.\n\nSources agree on the winners and the citation. The 2025 chemistry prize went to Susumu Kitagawa, Richard Robson and Omar Yaghi for metal-organic frameworks."], "durationSeconds": 5.613939874999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01RDrgXMW8U1NyNR7CD84i53", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
